  "finding": "Startup omitted a cache-check deadline. openActive initialized directories before cancellable reads, and the OPFS adapter retained its root promise across operations, including pending/failing results.",
  "contract": {
    "startup": "Existing operation-lifetime helper supplies one 60000ms cache-verification deadline through openActive's signal. Late success/failure is ignored and observed; timer resources are disposed.",
    "readOnly": "openActive performs no initialization; read resolution uses create:false. Writers still initialize with create:true. OPFS root resolution is independent per operation, with no shared rootPromise.",
    "userOutcome": "Timeout appears in both the simple error panel and chooser. No cache bytes are removed. Cache or cached-activation failure suppresses automatic replacement acquisition pending explicit user action. Verified empty caches still use automatic eligible MiniModel seeding; successfully activated saved models return to chat.",
    "unchanged": "Current six-member schemas, qualification gates, commit reconciliation, visual markup and runtime artifact bytes.",
    "limits": "60000ms is an asynchronous-wait policy, not a measured real-model performance budget or preemption of synchronous/suspended execution. No new deadlines for durable mutation or postcommit reconciliation."
  },
